# Design Specification: Android SMS Transaction Auto-Sync (Refined)

This document specifies the refined architecture and logic to automatically detect, parse, and log expenses from transaction SMS messages on Android.

---

## 1. Flow Overview & SMS Trigger

1. **Background Monitoring:** The Android application runs a background `BroadcastReceiver` listening for `android.provider.Telephony.SMS_RECEIVED`.
2. **Initial Filter:** The local code checks for transaction indicators (e.g., matching keywords like `Sent`, `Debited`, `Paid`, `Charged`, `Rs.`, `$`).
3. **Data Extraction:** If matched, the SMS body is sent to a local parser or a Supabase Edge Function to extract:
   * **Amount** (e.g., `30.00`)
   * **Date & Time** of receipt (e.g., `2026-07-25 17:56:00`)
   * **Location Coordinates** (cached at the exact moment the SMS is received, if location permission is granted)
   * **Recipient VPA / UPI ID** (e.g., `paytmqr6h6pev@ptys` or `swiggy@icici`)

---

## 2. VPA Categorization & Logic Matrix

When a VPA is extracted, the VPA handle (before the `@`) and the bank/provider (after the `@`) are split to determine the categorization path:

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Extracted VPA] --> B(Split VPA: handle@provider)
    
    B --> C{Is Personal/P2P?}
    C -->|Yes: Provider starts with 'ok' OR Handle is 10-digit number| D[Auto-save as 'Personal']
    
    C -->|No| E{Is Dynamic QR / Unrecognizable?}
    E -->|Yes: Handle contains 'qr' OR is alphanumeric hash| F[Check merchant_mappings table]
    
    F -->|Found mapping| G[Save with mapped Name & Category]
    F -->|Not found| H[Create PENDING Expense & Send Notification]
    
    E -->|No: Other handles e.g., swiggy@icici| I[Run Gemini Auto-Categorize]
    I --> J[Save automatically as Known Brand]
```

### Detailed Rules:

| VPA Type | Rules / Patterns | Resolution Path | Target Category |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Personal / P2P** | 1. Provider starts with `ok` (e.g., `oksbi`, `okaxis`, `okicici`).<br>2. Handle is exactly 10 numeric digits (e.g., `9876543210@paytm`). | Save immediately. | **Personal** |
| **Dynamic QR (Unrecognizable)** | Handle contains `qr` (e.g., `paytmqr...`) or is an alphanumeric hash (e.g., `paytmqr63o@ptys`). | **1. Check `merchant_mappings`:** If mapped in past, fetch friendly name & category.<br>**2. If Unmapped:** Notify user for quick input $\rightarrow$ If no input, save as **Pending**. | *Mapped Category* / **Pending** |
| **Known Brand / Named VPA** | Any other structured handle (e.g., `swiggy@icici`, `uber@icici`, `netflix@hdfc`). | Run Gemini OCR/Text parser $\rightarrow$ Save immediately. | **Auto-categorized** (e.g., Food, Transport) |

