## 5. UI Design for Pending Expenses

When there are pending transactions (under 24 hours old), the app guides the user to process them cleanly:

### 1. Home Screen Badge & Trigger
* A subtle but visible widget on the Home Page displays: `"You have 3 unprocessed transactions"`.
* Clicking this opens the **Quick Processing Carousel**.

### 2. Contextual Aids (Location & Time)
To jog the user's memory, cards are decorated with context:
* **Time:** *"Today at 2:14 PM"* or *"Yesterday at 8:30 AM"*.
* **Geographic Tags:** If coordinates were captured at the time the SMS was received, the app performs a local reverse-geocode lookup to display: *"Spent near Sector 62, Noida"* or *"Spent near Central Park"*.

### 3. Quick-Processing Modal
A sequential flashcard interface:
```
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|                  PENDING TRANSACTIONS               |
|                                                     |
|  [ Card 1 of 3 ]                                    |
|  Amount: Rs. 30.00                                  |
|  Time: Today, 2:14 PM                               |
|  Location: Near Sector 62, Noida                    |
|                                                     |
|  Who did you pay?                                   |
|  [ Raju Tea Stall                     ]             |
|                                                     |
|  Category:                                          |
|  ( ) Food    ( ) Transport    ( ) Shopping    (...) |
|                                                     |
|               [ SAVE ]      [ SKIP ]                |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
```

### 4. The 10-Second Auto-Popup Rule
* If the user opens the app and has pending items, we wait **10 seconds** of activity/idle on the home screen.
* If they don't click the banner, the Quick-Processing Modal automatically slides up to capture their feedback.
* **Frequency Limit:** This popup should only occur once per app session to avoid annoying the user if they actively dismiss it.

### 5. Daily Inactive Reminders
* At the end of the day (e.g., 9:00 PM), the app checks if there are unprocessed transactions and sends a single summary notification: *"You have 3 transactions from today that need categorizing. Tap to finish your daily budget."*

